  "contentHtml": "\n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p><a href=\"/tag/berhampur\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Berhampur</a>: A team of researchers from Indian Institute of Science Education and Research (IISER), Berhampur, has developed a <a href=\"/tag/nanotechnology-based+fluorescent+sensor\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">nanotechnology-based fluorescent sensor</a> which will enable faster detection and stratification of <a href=\"/tag/diabetic+kidney+disease+%28dkd%29\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">diabetic kidney disease (DKD)</a> using <a href=\"/tag/urine+samples\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">urine samples</a>.Differentiating diabetic kidney disease from other kidney disorders can be challenging due to overlapping clinical features, highlighting the need for faster and more specific approaches. The new nanotechnology sensor will offer potential for rapid, minimally invasive biomarker-based assessment with further validation, the researchers said.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M -->\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>“The study demonstrates a proof-of-concept for using a <a href=\"/tag/cof-based+fluorescent+immunosensor\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">COF-based fluorescent immunosensor</a> to detect <a href=\"/tag/ngal\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NGAL</a>, which is a protein and distinguishes diabetic kidney disease samples from other clinical groups,” said <a href=\"/tag/satyabrata+senapati\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Satyabrata Senapati</a>, research scholar and one of the authors of the article published in the ‘<a href=\"/tag/royal+society+of+chemistry\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Royal Society of Chemistry</a>’.“The technology is not intended to replace established diagnostic methods at this stage, but provides a promising platform for further optimisation and clinical validation,” said <a href=\"/tag/parikshit+moitra\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Parikshit Moitra</a>, assistant professor, Department of Chemical Sciences, who led the study.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Hrusikesh Mohanty</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Hrusikesh Mohanty</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/87654367/TNN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TNN</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Oct 6, 2026 at 04:30 PM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Oct 6, 2026 at 04:30 PM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">1 min read</li> -->\n                              